            "title": "Our forecast for 2019 U.S. real GDP growth has fallen slightly to 2.4%",
            "snippets": [
              "# Our forecast for 2019 U.S. real GDP growth has fallen slightly to 2.4%\n### Key Takeaways\n- **Our forecast for 2019 U.S. real GDP growth has fallen slightly to 2.4%.** Economic growth is shaping up to be weak in the first quarter; our most recent estimate is annualized growth of just 1.3%. The government component of GDP will likely weigh on growth in a transitory manner due to the shutdown, but private sector demand from personal consumption, housing and business investment has also looked soft",
              "### U.S. Growth Outlook\nWeaker government spending will also give way to weaker Q1 growth as a result of the government shutdown, but will likely be offset by a corresponding boost in the second quarter.\n- Real GDP growth forecast for full-year 2019: 2.4% (2.5% Q4-over-Q4)\n- **Change since last Monthly Economic Outlook: -0.1 percentage point**",
              "**Key Themes and Upside/Downside Scenarios**\n\n- Growth set to continue in 2019, albeit at a more modest pace.\n- Upside scenario: A trade deal is reached, erasing some uncertainty and boosting the global growth backdrop, while Goldilocks inflation keeps the Fed from needing to tighten monetary policy too quickly",
              "- Downside scenario: The lagged effect of higher interest rates pressures consumers and businesses, while a full-blown trade war weighs on confidence and global growth, causing economic growth in the United States to slow more sharply than we currently expect"
            ]
